From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:59:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] CfgRecord: the status text, five stale docstring passages,
 and `recordStep_cell_write` through `Action.apply`'s field equation

Maintainer commit at integration (the review's F2, F3, F4; the user's rulings of 2026-10-22):
- the module's status paragraph: all three rows compose the framed rows through their contracts;
- the docstrings that still named the retired `RecordRun`, `recordRun_trans` and
  `compareTM_run_ofCfg`, and "Unfold `Turing.Cfg.init`", now name what the proofs use;
- `recordStep_cell_write` closed only because `Action.apply` is `@[simp]`; it now reads the
  action through `Action.apply_workTapes` (the review's tested re-proof);
- two private docstrings reworded, and one "Proof sketch" added.
Code otherwise unchanged; the module elaborates with no output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
